    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδάμ-αστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unsubdued, inflexible</i>, of Hades, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.158
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>D.</u>
				1.18
			</span></i>: later in the proper sense, <i>untamed, unbroken</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				20
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πᾶσιν</span> Timo<i><span class="en">
				9.1
			</span></i>.</div>
